[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Pawn Game"]
[Variation "Colle System, Qb3 mistake"]
[ECO "D05"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap"]
[Themes "pawn-fork,queen-and-bishop"]
[Refutes "1. d4 d5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. e3 e6 4. Bd3 c5 5. c3 Nc6 6. Qb3"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "for-us"]
[Opponent "6.Qb3"]
[Start "1. d4 d5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. e3 e6 4. Bd3 c5 5. c3 Nc6"]

6. Qb3 $2 { White hits b7 and d5 and forgets that the queen and the bishop on d3 sit on the same diagonal. } 6... c4 { A pawn attacks the queen and the bishop at once. White cannot save both. } 7. Bxc4 ( 7. Bc2 cxb3 { The queen is simply lost. } ) 7... dxc4 8. Qxc4 Bd6 { Black has a bishop for two pawns, the bishop pair, and the quicker development, with White's king still in the centre. } 9. O-O O-O *
